SDK DPAA dpaa_eth_sg.c: provide skb_recycle() shim

drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/sdk_dpaa/dpaa_eth_sg.c calls skb_recycle()
in the TX recycle fast-path (line 1210).  skb_recycle() was removed from
mainline years ago (commit e6da78f in 4.x).

  drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/sdk_dpaa/dpaa_eth_sg.c:1210:17:
    error: implicit declaration of function 'skb_recycle'

Provide a static inline equivalent that performs the parts of the old
helper the SDK actually relies on:
  - skb_release_head_state()
  - reset shinfo and dataref
  - zero the skb up to ->tail

The caller immediately overrides skb->data and tailptr after the call,
so we don't replicate skb_recycle's NET_SKB_PAD reservation (the comment
already in the SDK source notes this explicitly).

--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/sdk_dpaa/dpaa_eth_sg.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/sdk_dpaa/dpaa_eth_sg.c
@@ -45,6 +45,25 @@
 #include <linux/fsl_bman.h>
 #include <net/sock.h>
 
+/*
+ * skb_recycle() was removed from mainline; the SDK still calls it.
+ * Provide a static inline equivalent: release head state, reset
+ * shinfo refcount, zero the skb up to ->tail.  The caller (this file
+ * at the only call site) immediately overrides skb->data and tailptr
+ * so we don't bother setting them here.
+ */
+static inline void skb_recycle(struct sk_buff *skb)
+{
+	struct skb_shared_info *shinfo;
+
+	skb_release_head_state(skb);
+	shinfo = skb_shinfo(skb);
+	memset(shinfo, 0, offsetof(struct skb_shared_info, dataref));
+	atomic_set(&shinfo->dataref, 1);
+	memset(skb, 0, offsetof(struct sk_buff, tail));
+}
+
+
 #include "dpaa_eth.h"
 #include "dpaa_eth_common.h"
 #ifdef CONFIG_FSL_DPAA_1588
